# Safety and Scope

## Authorized System

- Host: `SOC-WIN11`
- Platform: Windows 11 ARM
- Hypervisor: UTM
- Environment: Personal isolated lab


---


## Authorized Techniques

| Validation | Technique | Approved behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| VAL-001 | T1082 | Read basic system details |
| VAL-002 | T1016 | Read local network configuration |
| VAL-003 | T1059.003 | Create or display harmless text through command shell |
| VAL-004 | T1027 | Run reviewed PowerShell that prints harmless text |


---


## Prohibited Activity

- Credential dumping or LSASS access
- Mimikatz
- Process injection
- Persistence
- Ransomware simulation
- UAC bypass
- Remote execution
- Browser credential extraction
- Defender or firewall disabling
- Destructive activity
- Real malware
- Unknown payload downloads
- Unreviewed tests
- Execution outside the lab VM


---


## Safety Controls

| Control | Reason |
|---|---|
| Pre-test UTM snapshot | Provides rollback |
| Defender remains enabled | Avoids weakening the environment |
| Exact test review | Prevents accidental execution |
| Specific test number only | Avoids running an entire technique |
| Recorded test window | Supports accurate evidence collection |
| Cleanup reviewed first | Confirms reversibility |
| Cleanup verification | Proves endpoint recovery |


---


## Stop Conditions

Stop when the system identity is wrong, the test definition differs, an unknown download appears, a security exclusion is requested, or cleanup cannot be explained.

---


## Recovery Plan

1. Stop further execution.
2. Record the unexpected result.
3. Run reviewed cleanup when safe.
4. Verify files, processes, services, Defender, and Sysmon.
5. Restore `PRE-WEEK8-ATOMIC-TESTING` when cleanup cannot return the VM to baseline.
